The Higher People's Court of Heilongjiang Province:
Your Request for Instructions on How to Confirm the Validity of Loan Contracts Between Citizens and Enterprises (Hei Gao Fa [1998] No. 192) has been received. Upon study, the reply is as follows:
Loans between citizens and non-financial enterprises (hereinafter referred to as "enterprises") constitute private lending. A loan shall be deemed valid as long as the true intention of both parties is expressed. However, it shall be deemed invalid under any of the following circumstances:
(1) the enterprise illegally raises funds from its employees in the name of lending;
(2) the enterprise illegally raises funds from the public in the name of lending;
(3) the enterprise extends loans to the public in the name of lending;
(4) other acts that violate laws or administrative regulations.
Where the lending interest rate exceeds four times the interest rate of similar loans offered by banks during the same period, the matter shall be handled in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Supreme People's Court's Several Opinions on the Trial of Lending Cases (Fa (Min) Fa [1991] No. 21).
This is in reply.
